      "id": 18301,
      "name": "bjorn.arnesen.us",
      "username": "bjorn.arnesen.us",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-08-02T14:35:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I just received my physical copy of OblivAeon yesterday, and have already submitted an OblivAeon game for a coming gaming convention.</p><p>There are a couple \"removed from game\" cases that raise interesting questions.</p><p>If a player is incapacitated as Stuntman after using \"In Media Res\", if that player chooses Stuntman's variant as their next hero, is that card added back to the game?</p><p>Given Ra's variants, I'm considering a house rule that you can play the other two versions of Ra in any order, but Setting Sun must be last. Let's say I don't apply that house rule. Would cards removed from the game by Setting Sun's base power be added back when the player chose another version of Ra?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:36.038Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
