      "id": 220869,
      "name": "Legend of Ruina",
      "username": "Joebobjoe",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/dec6dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2018-09-14T14:57:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Yes, the thing being that the Aeon Warrior is the only one without an easy answer to what happens if Oblivaeon destroys it remotely. Admittedly Aeon Thralls may be affected by the ruling as well, but at least have an easily apparent answer. The effect of an Aeon Warrior makes Oblivaeon himself hit the highest HP Hero target when he destroys it. The question is what happens if this occurs while Oblivaeon is in a different zone from the Warrior. Used Aeon Master as the example because it was the only one that occurred to me at the time, suppose Global Devastation could also do it.</p>",
      "post_number": 10,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:53:26.040Z",
